# Temperance marker — sync/v1.0.0-substrate

- date: 2026-09-21
- branch: sync/v1.0.0-substrate
- scope-decision: Refresh `dist/lite/` bundled substrate from public bassclef v1.0.0 (commit `1fcd6ed9`), bump `@thebassclef/lite` from 1.2.2 to 1.3.0, stage PR for operator merge + tag + publish.
- right-thing: Yes. Public bassclef v1.0.0 shipped 2026-09-20T23:34Z with Ship 1 install-class boundary cures (retag 3 operator-only files, prune 33 dead hook wirings, sanitize 30 hardcoded paths). Adopter tarball at 1.2.2 still ships v0.46.0 substrate.
- right-way: Rebuild dist/lite from public bassclef sibling. Tests green (433 of 433). Version bump to 1.3.0. Commit. Stage PR. Operator merges + tags. Publish workflow fires on release event. Docker harness picks up new tarball automatically.
- blast-radius: Adopter-observable. New tarball reaches every fresh `npm install -g @thebassclef/lite` adopter. Reversible via `npm deprecate` or bump-and-fix (1.3.1) within the 72h unpublish window.
- drift-trigger: If test suite regresses after substrate refresh, pause and diagnose before commit. If dist/lite layout changes shape (new top-level dirs, missing `.claude/`), pause and verify against wiring manifest.
- upstream-dependency: Public bassclef `1fcd6ed9` (tag v1.0.0) is the source of truth. No dependency on unmerged upstream work. F1b and F4 cures deferred to v1.1.0 substrate refresh in a separate future PR.
